# CloudSentinel does not use a .env file for the deployed Lambdas — their
# configuration comes entirely from Terraform (see
# terraform/modules/detection/main.tf's `environment { variables = {...} }`
# blocks and IAM_DESIGN.md). This file only documents the shell environment
# variables the DEVELOPMENT tooling (pytest, the AWS CLI) actually reads.
#
# Copy to .env and `source .env` (or export manually) if you want these set
# for your shell — nothing in this project loads .env automatically.

# Set to 1 to force every test in tests/live/ to skip, even with a real
# deployment and valid credentials present — e.g. to run the full suite
# quickly with zero AWS API calls. See tests/live/conftest.py.
# CLOUDSENTINEL_SKIP_LIVE=1

# Standard AWS CLI/boto3 variable — which named profile scripts/*.sh and
# tests/live/ should use. Leave unset to use your default profile/credentials.
# AWS_PROFILE=your-profile-name
